>> Junk artifacts.
>
> I'm particularly annoyed by the ones that destroy
> monster inventory (why would I ever want that?),

The ones that destroy items are also the ones that do a lot of extra
damage.  Classic Nethack condundrum.

> but also a lot of even the supposedly good artifacts
> have relatively small bonuses or only get their
> bonus against a very strictly limited set of opponents.

The ones that only add damage based on class tend to be considered junk.
Orcrist might not be junk in the mines but by Medusa it is.  Demonbane
might be junk in the mines but it's not below the VofD.  Trollsbane,
though, junk almost every point of every game.

>> Sling as not a commonly used weapon
>
> The big problem with a sling is that you
> can't use it while wielding a melee weapon.
> (It shares this property with the bow.)

This is one reason why daggers are so well loved.

> In combat, when an enemy closes to
> melee range, I typically do NOT want
> to spend a turn switching weapons.  For
> this reason I favor darts (if my role can
> get skill in them) or daggers (if my role
> can't get skill in darts but can in dagger).

The other reason is daggers are the multifire class that does not
disappear.  Darts have a finite source and they disappear.

> Also, playing in what basically amounts
> to a cave, you wouldn't think you'd have
> any trouble finding rocks, but I've had
> serious running-out-of-ammo problems
> when playing as a caveman.  I think
> it's because the rocks have a higher
> probability (than darts or especially
> daggers) of disappearing after just
> one use.

When is it ever worth blessing a stack of rocks?  Blessed ammo
disappears less often.  In games that I don't use a sling there are more
rocks than I could possibly shuttle around.  Funny hows that works.


